## Page 13

::: {#exm-variance-formula}

### Variance Calculation
Example of rewriting the sum of squared differences:

$$
\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\overline{X})^{2} = \sum_{i=1}^{n}{x_{i}}^{2}-n\cdot\overline{x}^{2}
$$

:::

## Page 14

Sum of squares calculation continuation:

$$
\sum (x_i - \overline{x})^2 = 2
$$

When values are extremely large (e.g., $10^{12}$), floating-point precision loss occurs:

$$
(\sum x_i)^2 = (6M+6)^2 \approx 12M^2
$$

